---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Support — LimeBeam"
  description="Help and contact for LimeBeam, an IPTV player for your Xtream and M3U playlists."
  altHref="/support"
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p class="lead">A question, a bug, an idea? Drop us a line — we reply.</p>

  <a class="btn" href="mailto:clement@stairling.com">Contact us</a>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <div class="card">
    <strong>Does LimeBeam provide channels or content?</strong>
    <p class="muted">
      No. LimeBeam is a player: you connect your own IPTV subscription via an
      Xtream Codes account or an M3U / M3U8 playlist.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <strong>How can I try the app without a subscription?</strong>
    <p class="muted">
      On the welcome screen, tap "Try the demo": a small set of free, public
      test streams loads with no credentials at all.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <strong>Where are my credentials stored?</strong>
    <p class="muted">
      On your device only (system secure storage). Nothing is sent to the
      publisher. See the <a href="/en/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <strong>What are tips for?</strong>
    <p class="muted">
      They support development, nothing more. They unlock no content or feature.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
